.ad l
.SH NAME
xara \- VARA\-compatible HF/FM modem
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]xara\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-audio pulse\f[R]|\f[B]alsa\f[R]]
\f[B]\-\-call\f[R] \f[I]CALL\f[R] \f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] \f[I]SOURCE\f[R]
\f[B]\-\-playback\f[R] \f[I]SINK\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]xara\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-audio pulse\f[R]|\f[B]alsa\f[R]] \f[B]\-\-radio
\-\-ptt\f[R] \f[I]PTT\f[R] \f[B]\-\-call\f[R] \f[I]CALL\f[R]
\f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] \f[I]SOURCE\f[R] \f[B]\-\-playback\f[R]
\f[I]SINK\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]xara\f[R] is a modem compatible with VARA HF and VARA FM.
It supports audio via ALSA and PipeWire/Pulse.
It also exposes TCP ports for VARA\(aqs command and data along with KISS
for applications such as Pat.
See the README for full details.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-config\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
Read options from \f[I]FILE\f[R].
Any options given on the command line override these.
Each line in the file is one option without its leading dashes:
\f[I]key\f[R] \f[B]=\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R].
For example, \f[B]capture = plughw:CARD=Device,DEV=0\f[R].
Repeated keys are treated the same way as repeated options.
.RS
.PP
Without \f[B]\-\-config\f[R], xara reads
\f[I]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xara/xara.conf\f[R] (by default
\f[I]\(ti/.config/xara/xara.conf\f[R]) if it exists.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-audio\f[R] pulse|alsa
Audio backend.
Defaults to Pulse if compiled in, otherwise ALSA.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] \f[I]SOURCE\f[R]
Pulse source or ALSA PCM to receive from (required).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-playback\f[R] \f[I]SINK\f[R]
Pulse sink or ALSA PCM to transmit into (required).
Without \f[B]\-\-radio\f[R], it must be a Pulse null sink or the ALSA
\f[B]null\f[R] PCM.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-tx\-buffer\-ms\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Transmit audio queued ahead of the sound card, in ms.
30\-500 (default 40).
Raise it if xara logs playback underruns: try 80, then 160.
xara times its transmissions around the extra delay, but keep it as low
as runs without underruns.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-call\f[R] \f[I]CALL\f[R]
Initial MYCALL (required; N0CALL is refused).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-hf\f[R] 500|2300|2750
Run as VARA HF with this bandwidth (default 2300); not with
\f[B]\-\-fm\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-fm\f[R] narrow|wide
Run as VARA FM instead of HF.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-digi\f[R] \f[I]CALL\f[R]
FM only: also digipeat for \f[I]CALL\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-record\f[R] \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Record RX, TX, and PTT to FLAC (or WAV if filename ends in .wav).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-port\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Command port (default 8300); data is on \f[I]N\f[R]+1.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-kiss\-port\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]|off
KISS TCP port (default 8100).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-persistence\f[R] \f[I]P\f[R]
KISS p\-persistence, 0 to 1 (default 0.3).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-addr\f[R] \f[I]A\f[R]
Listen address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-drive\-db\f[R] \f[I]D\f[R]
TX drive in dB, at most 0 (default \-5).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-log\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
Append UTC\-timestamped output to \f[I]FILE\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-quiet\f[R]
No trace output.
Lines are still logged when using \f[B]\-\-log\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-port\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Serve the web UI on port \f[I]N\f[R]: with bonus data at
\f[B]/stream\f[R].
Off by default.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-addr\f[R] \f[I]A\f[R]
Web UI listen address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-host\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Also accept \f[I]NAME\f[R] in the HTTP Host header (repeatable).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-control\f[R]
\f[B]DANGER\f[R] allows a remote web user with the UI token to key the
radio, make config changes, and generally ruin your day.
Be careful when allowing.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-state\-dir\f[R] \f[I]DIR\f[R]
Where to keep settings saved from the web UI.
Defaults to \f[B]$STATE_DIRECTORY\f[R] when launched with systemd.
If not included, settings are not saved.
Web settings override command line parameters, which override config
file entries.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-token\f[R] \f[I]T\f[R]
UI secret key required to remotely control the rig.
If not supplied, xara generates a random token and keeps it in
\f[I]DIR\f[R]/ui\-token.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-radio\f[R]
Transmit over a real radio.
Requires \f[B]\-\-ptt\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ptt\f[R] \f[I]PTT\f[R]
PTT method; requires \f[B]\-\-radio\f[R].
One of \f[B]vox\f[R] \f[B]rts:\f[R]\f[I]DEV\f[R] or
\f[B]dtr:\f[R]\f[I]DEV\f[R], \f[B]cm108:\f[R]\f[I]DEV[:GPIO]\f[R], or
\f[B]rigctld\f[R][\f[B]:\f[R]\f[I]HOST\f[R]\f[B]:\f[R]\f[I]PORT\f[R]].
For full details see README.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ptt\-lead\-ms\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Hold PTT for N ms before transmit.
0\-1000 (default 0).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ptt\-tail\-ms\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Hold PTT for N ms after transmit.
0\-1000 (default 100).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ptt\-max\-s\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Release PTT after \f[I]N\f[R] seconds max, 1\-120 (default 30).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-registered\f[R]
Enable registered speeds (must set build flag)
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R], \f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the usage or the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Normal exit.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
PTT error (including failed release), or audio, device or port error.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Bad command line.
.TP
\f[B]75\f[R]
A restart asked for from the web UI could not re\-execute xara; a
service manager should start it again.
.TP
\f[B]101\f[R]
Stopped after a panic.
PTT will have been released.
.TP
\f[B]130\f[R]
Stopped by SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP or SIGQUIT.
PTT will have been released
.SH SAFETY
If you kill with SIGKILL, PTT may not be released!
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]/etc/xara/STATION.conf\f[R]
The config file of the \f[B]xara\(atSTATION\f[R] system service.
Must be readable by the \f[B]xara\f[R] user (mode 0640 recommended if it
contains \f[B]ui\-token\f[R]).
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.config/xara/xara.conf\f[R]
The config file of the \f[B]xara\f[R] user service and used when xara is
run without \f[B]\-\-config\f[R].
.TP
\f[I]/var/lib/xara/STATION/settings\f[R]
Settings saved from the web UI for \f[B]xara\(atSTATION\f[R]
(\f[I]\(ti/.local/state/xara/settings\f[R] for the user service).
One \f[I]key\f[R] \f[B]=\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R] per line, and the keys are
the options without their leading dashes.
.TP
\f[I]/var/lib/xara/STATION/ui\-token\f[R]
The web UI token if \f[B]\-\-ui\-token\f[R] is not provided on the
command line.
\f[I]\(ti/.local/state/xara/ui\-token\f[R] for the user service.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]XARA_UI_TOKEN\f[R]
The web UI token xara passes to itself when it restarts if
\f[B]\-\-ui\-token\f[R] is not provided on the command line.
.TP
\f[B]STATE_DIRECTORY\f[R]
Used as \f[B]\-\-state\-dir\f[R] if that is not included on command
line.
systemd sets it from \f[B]StateDirectory=\f[R].
